As with the scythe and flail it was never really intended as a weapon
in the first place.  It's a farming implement that happened to be at
hand when the call for battle came out.  When the call for battle
comes you grab whatever is close by that you think might work
better than bare hands and that's what you use.  The blacksmith
grabs a hammer, the fieldsman grabs a pole sickle, the barnsman
grabs a flail, the miner grabs a pickaxe, the mason grabs a brick.



